  "note": "bounded(1,2) KNOWS Expand \u2014 a NODE relation deduplicated at minimum depth (\u00a72.3), which is exactly the reference's `WITH DISTINCT friend`, and whose a=1 floor is also what drops the start person -> exact(1) HAS_MEMBER dir=in with edge_var=membership -> PropertyPredicate(joinDate > $minDate). That membership relation is folded two ways: a DISTINCT forum set (Aggregate(group_by=[forumId, forumTitle], aggregates=[])) and a DISTINCT (forum, friend) cohort probe. The post branch expands CONTAINER_OF/HAS_CREATOR off the forum set, semi-joins the friend cohort (\u00a72.8, Join{inner} on (forum, creator)), and Aggregate(group_by=[forum], count) counts it; then Join{left_outer} back onto the forum set and Project(postCount := coalesce(pc, 0)) (R2). **The coalesce rewrite is required**: \u00a72.10 defines no null-skipping aggregate, so a bare `count` over a left_outer null would return 1 where the reference returns 0 \u2014 and postCount is the sort key under the Limit(20). FREEZE \u00a77.6 declares this shape in advance (aggregate the inner join first, then left_outer back onto the full left side, then coalesce in a row-local Project) as the predicted plan for the four rows that depend on it. Sole residual was `var-length-bounded`, in v1 under R6/R5 (\u00a72.3 `bounded(1,2)`, \u00a74.3 bind-time).",
  "compilation_note": "FAITHFUL TO THE FORECAST ROUTE. The `Project` beneath the `Join{inner}` builds the join keys, which \u00a72.8 blesses explicitly ('keys are identity-typed or scalar-typed columns, or a `tuple(...)` built in `Project`') \u2014 it is part of the route, not a workaround. An earlier revision of this note justified it by a defect instead (`eval_join` asserted its realized schema equalled the node's declared one, which column pruning legitimately violates); that defect was fixed in M3.5 and the justification is corrected here. The plan itself is unchanged, and so are its rows."
